<title>USA: Egypt to upgrade anti-aircraft missiles.</title>
<headline>Egypt to upgrade anti-aircraft missiles.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States plans to upgrade Egypt's &quot;Hawk&quot; anti-aircraft missile system for an estimated $303 million, the Defence Department said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The prime contractor on the work to upgrade ground equipment and install modification kits for the U.S.-built surface-to-air missiles would be Raytheon Co., the Pentagon said.</p>
<p>In a separate brief announcement, the department said that the United States also planned to sell 314 AIM-9M &quot;Sidewinder&quot; air-to-air missiles, built by Raytheon, to Egypt for $34 million.</p>
</text>
